00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:01.890
Hello and welcome.

00:00:02.430 --> 00:00:07.230
In this video, we will look at what constitutes
a hazard and risk in the workplace, what they

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:09.210
are, and how they're different from each other.

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:12.090
So what are hazards?

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:15.840
A hazard can be defined as
anything that may cause harm.

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:21.630
For example, anything that might cause a trip
or fall, such as wires loose on the floor.

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:26.280
Working with electricity is a
hazard, as is working with machines,

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:29.070
tools, ladders and lifting items.

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:31.920
So what is a risk?

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:36.780
Risks can be defined as the potential
harm that a hazard has associated with it.

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:41.910
If we look again at the example of leaving
wiring loose on the floor, this is a hazard

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:44.220
with a very high risk that it could cause harm.

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:48.390
It's important that employers
carry out risk assessments.

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:53.460
These are checks to see what safety measures
or changes should be implemented to lower

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:55.519
the risk and reduce the chance of harm.

00:00:57.410 --> 00:00:59.865
As an example, let's have a look at this image.

00:01:00.645 --> 00:01:04.965
I think we can all agree that standing on
a forklift to reach a high box is a hazard.

00:01:05.805 --> 00:01:10.020
The person may not fall, but it's likely
that they will, and this likelihood

00:01:10.575 --> 00:01:12.255
determines the level of the risk.

00:01:12.825 --> 00:01:16.215
In this case, the activity
would be classed as high risk.

00:01:17.535 --> 00:01:21.975
As you can see in this new image, measures
have been brought in to reduce the risk.

00:01:22.605 --> 00:01:27.524
Using a ladder is still a hazard as there's
still a risk of falling, but it's less likely.

00:01:28.065 --> 00:01:32.955
Therefore, although using a ladder is still
a hazard, there is minimal risk involved.

00:01:34.905 --> 00:01:38.535
So what about other hazards and risks
that you may encounter in the workplace?

00:01:39.104 --> 00:01:40.515
Let's take a look at some of these.

00:01:41.775 --> 00:01:44.414
DSE stands for display Screen Equipment.

00:01:45.405 --> 00:01:51.085
Sitting in front of a computer may seem harmless,
but there are several hazards to consider such as.

00:01:51.885 --> 00:01:58.665
Repetitive strain injury RSI from typing for
long periods of time, back and or shoulder

00:01:58.665 --> 00:02:03.075
pain from sitting in one position for too
long, or sitting with incorrect posture.

00:02:03.915 --> 00:02:08.205
Eye damage from screen glare, and
spending too long staring at a monitor.

00:02:09.495 --> 00:02:14.945
These hazards become a greater risk depending
on how the computer desk and chair are position.

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:20.160
As you can see in this image, the equipment
is not set up correctly, which may result

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:23.640
in the user experiencing some of the
health issues we have already mentioned.

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:28.560
It is important that the computer desk
and chair are set up correctly as shown

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:33.990
in this second image, a DSE workstation
assessment should be carried out and

00:02:33.990 --> 00:02:38.730
training provided on ways to minimize any
potential health risks, such as taking

00:02:38.730 --> 00:02:41.210
regular breaks or doing something different.

00:02:43.065 --> 00:02:47.355
Lifting anything of weight or size is
hazardous and can be considered a high

00:02:47.359 --> 00:02:53.114
risk activity as serious injuries may be
incurred to the spine, ligaments and tendons.

00:02:54.345 --> 00:02:59.295
Also, heavier and bulkier items are more
hazardous and carry greater the risk for injury.

00:02:59.864 --> 00:03:05.325
It's therefore imperative to know how to lift
safely or use mechanical lifting aids if needed.

00:03:06.285 --> 00:03:10.484
As you can see from these two images, the
right and the wrong way to lift an object.

00:03:12.645 --> 00:03:17.375
Many substances used within the workplace
are hazardous, and it's not just chemicals

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:21.465
used in production, machinery and
engineering that you need to be aware of.

00:03:22.005 --> 00:03:26.505
Cleaning products, photocopier  toner,
and some other general office supplies

00:03:26.505 --> 00:03:28.185
are also considered hazardous.

00:03:28.935 --> 00:03:31.454
The more toxic the substance, the higher the risk.

00:03:32.144 --> 00:03:36.255
We all use cleaning products within our
home, so the risk here is quite minimal.

00:03:36.825 --> 00:03:42.239
However, if you are using these all day, every
day, as an industrial cleaner, the risk is greater

00:03:42.239 --> 00:03:47.940
and personal protective equipment PPE should be
worn, such as gloves, overalls, and face masks.

